  <example number="7.62">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor completely: $$12y^{2} - 75$$ .</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
            <cell>Yes, 3.</cell>
            <cell>$$12y^{2} - 75$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$3\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more than three terms?</cell>
            <cell>Binomial.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is it a sum?</cell>
            <cell>No.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is it a difference? Of squares or cubes?</cell>
            <cell>Yes, squares.</cell>
            <cell>$$3\left( {\left( {2y} \right)^{2} - (5)^{2}} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Write as a product of conjugates.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$3\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is the expression factored completely?</cell>
            <cell>Yes.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Neither binomial is a difference of squares.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply. $$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ { 3\left( {2y - 5} \right)\left( {2y + 5} \right)} \\ { 3\left( {4y^{2} - 25} \right)} \\ { 12y^{2} - 75 ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
