  <example number="7.64">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor completely: $$6y^{2} - 18y - 60$$ .</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
            <cell>Yes, 6.</cell>
            <cell>$$6y^{2} - 18y - 60$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$6\left( {y^{2} - 3y - 10} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more terms?</cell>
            <cell>Trinomial with leading coefficient 1.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>“Undo” FOIL.</cell>
            <cell>$$6\left( {y } \right)\left( {y } \right)$$</cell>
            <cell>$$6\left( {y + 2} \right)\left( {y - 5} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check your answer.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is the expression factored completely?</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>Yes.</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Neither binomial is a difference of squares.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply. $$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ { 6\left( {y + 2} \right)\left( {y - 5} \right)} \\ { 6\left( {y^{2} - 5y + 2y - 10} \right)} \\ { 6\left( {y^{2} - 3y - 10} \right)} \\ { 6y^{2} - 18y - 60 ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
