  <example number="7.67">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Factor completely: $$3x^{2} + 6bx - 3ax - 6ab$$ .</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell>Is there a GCF?</cell>
            <cell>Yes, 3.</cell>
            <cell>$$3x^{2} + 6bx - 3ax - 6ab$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Factor out the GCF.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$3\left( {x^{2} + 2bx - ax - 2ab} \right)$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>In the parentheses, is it a binomial, trinomial,or are there more terms?</cell>
            <cell>More than 3 terms.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Use grouping.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell>$$\begin{matrix} \\ {3\left\lbrack {x\left( {x + 2b} \right) - a\left( {x + 2b} \right)} \right\rbrack} \\ {3\left( {x + 2b} \right)\left( {x - a} \right)} \end{matrix}$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Check your answer.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Is the expression factored completely? Yes.</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply. $$\begin{array}{l} \\ \\ { 3\left( {x + 2b} \right)\left( {x - a} \right)} \\ { 3\left( {x^{2} - ax + 2bx - 2ab} \right)} \\ { 3x^{2} - 3ax + 6bx - 6ab ✓} \end{array}$$</cell>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </solution>
  </example>
